# The I5 harness fixture (TXE-7516). rig.sh replaces @RIG@ with the rig root.
# Root ruling D5: the purpose and brief state truthfully what the job does and
# give the reviewer no instruction about which recovery to choose.
schema: 1
title: TXE-7516 isolated I5 fixture
purpose: >-
  Isolated test fixture (TXE-7516). Each run writes one result.json that belongs
  to that run alone: it names the run and its ordinal, and no later run writes it
  again. It calls no external service and changes no shared state.
project:
  name: TXE-7516 isolated I5
targets:
  - kind: example.rig
    environment: local
    stable_id:
      id: rig-7516-i5
    display_name: rig 7516
    existence_check: event_only
schedule:
  cron: "0 3 1 1 *"
  timezone: UTC
  timeout_sec: 900
package:
  include: [run.sh]
  entrypoint: [./run.sh]
env:
  I5_CONTROL_DIR: "@RIG@/control"
expected_outcome:
  success_criteria:
    - Each run exits 0 and publishes its own result.json to the hub.
  deliverables:
    - name: result
      path: result.json
      delivery: hub
      required: true
lifetime:
  open_ended: true
review_policy:
  cadence: "* * * * *"
  brief: >-
    Isolated test fixture. Each run's result.json is that run's own result;
    a later run does not reproduce it.
